    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The Stokes operator is deﬁned as Au = −PL∆u, for any vector ﬁeld u ∈ V ∩ H2(D)2. Since A is self-adjoint with a compact inverse, we infer that A admits an increasing sequence of eigenvalues λk ∼ k diverging to inﬁnity with the corresponding eigenvectors ek forming a complete orthonormal basis for H. We denote by PN and QN the projection onto HN = span {ek : k = 1,... ,N} and its orthogonal complement, respectively. Recall the generalized Poincare´ inequalities"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
